[TOOL CALLING INSTRUCTIONS]
To call a tool, add it to `tool_calls` with its `name` and its arguments:
- `args`: the argument values, as an object. Set an argument you do not supply
  to null.
{% if json_argument_tools -%}
- `args_json`: these tools take `args_json` in place of `args`, the same object
  written as a JSON string: {{ json_argument_tools|join(", ") }}.
{% endif -%}
- `refs`: leave it empty when every argument is written out in `args`. Add an
  entry only for an argument whose value is taken from elsewhere: it names the
  argument (`arg`), where its value comes from (`source`) and the `key` to look
  up. Source "step" with the `call_id` of a tool call from an earlier step
  reuses that call's output; source "input" with the name of a context
  variable listed above uses that variable. The tool calls of one step run
  together, so a call cannot reference another call of its own step, and a call
  that ended in an error has no output to reference.
An argument appears in `args` or in `refs`, never in both. Set a `call_id` no
earlier call has used, so you can reference the result in later steps. The
output of each tool call is recorded in the steps listed in the last message.

When you have enough information to answer, set `output` to the final result and
leave `tool_calls` empty.
